+# #469: display the existing used Ink Storm gauge clock
+
+This is a dependent residual fix on PR #322, exact `9f1fcacb19c6f410742fefa3b521ad6579d97b7c`. That PR already owns Storm holding, the GP0 480-frame recharge lock, and its continuation through death and respawn. It does not display the remaining used-special gauge: native `_startSpecial()` spends the charge points immediately, and the Game HUD frame reads that zero through `specialFrac()`.
+
+The Actor now exposes a display snapshot derived from the same existing lock. It shows a full used gauge while the device is held, then `stormGaugeLock / STORM_GAUGE_LOCK` during the existing drain interval. Game projects the snapshot into its existing frame immediately before sending it to HUD and mobile controls, without allocating another per-frame object. The active style continues after the short throwing state ends. Ready state still comes from `specialReady()`, so a full-looking held gauge cannot be reused.
+
+There is no second countdown. `special`, `specialFrac()`, native network packet charge, refill blocking, death penalty, cloud damage, and the ordinary Slam display retain their existing owners. Spent charge remains zero on the wire; the local used-special display is deliberately a separate quantity. This does not add a remote drain-gauge protocol or claim hostile-owner Storm admission is fixed (#598).
+
+## Reference and scope
+
+The S3 verification page explicitly lists a 480F/8-second gauge lock and says the lock continues across death/respawn. This is independent evidence for the existing PR #322 constant, not an inference from rain lifetime:
+https://wikiwiki.jp/splatoon3mix/ブキ/スペシャルウェポン/アメフラシ
+
+The page's base-performance table is marked Ver.10.1.0; this patch does not introduce or re-calibrate timing for later versions or additional gear. It projects the existing actor-owned PR #322 clock. It does not change the unresolved exact throw-startup timing recorded by that dependency.
+
+## Validation
+
+The old #322 tree failed all three new baseline cases because it displayed zero during hold/drain and after respawn. Fixed source cases cover every one of the 480 lock ticks, held-device time, death/respawn, fresh actors, unchanged native packet charge, and ordinary charge/Slam controls. Actual native HUD `_updSpecial` is exercised with display element stand-ins: at half drain it shows 50%, the liquid transform is 50px, active remains set, and no ready or gain flashes occur. This is actual HUD logic in a VM, not a physical browser screenshot.
+
+- Source new tests: 6/6 passed.
+- Existing PR #322 source tests: 12/12 passed.
+- Actual minified output: 18/18 passed (all 6 new cases and 12 dependency cases).
+- Full gameplay/reliability suite on exact PR #322 stack: 761/761 passed, no skips.
+- Build content prefix: 0073f3045bda.
+
+## Integration conditions
+
+This stack is not part of the current PR #536 public tree and is not a claim that all of PR #322 is accepted. The integration review already identified two separate future-composition conditions: #322's `collectStormHit` transformation removes the current network recipient-dt anchor, and its `cloudCoversActor` still uses `dur - .3`, which needs reconciliation with #563's full-duration rain. This residual display patch does not resolve or bypass those conditions.
